in the Software without restriction, including without limitation the rights
to use, copy, modify, merge, publish, distribute, and sublicense copies of
the Software, subject to the following conditions:

1. The above copyright notice and this permission notice shall be included in
   all copies or substantial portions of the Software.

2. PROHIBITION ON AI TRAINING (Material Condition):
   The Software, and any derivative work as defined by copyright law that
   incorporates the Software or any substantial portion thereof, may NOT be
   used to train, fine-tune, distill, prompt-tune, or otherwise optimize any
   machine learning model, neural network, large language model, or
   artificial intelligence system. This prohibition applies regardless of
   whether the derivative work has been transformed, combined with other
   code, or modified.

3. DERIVATIVE INHERITANCE CLAUSE:
   Any person who receives a derivative work of this Software is bound by
   Condition 2 to the same extent as if they had received the original
   Software. Distribution of a derivative work without prominently
   displaying this prohibition constitutes willful inducement of breach.

4. LIQUIDATED DAMAGES AND CHARITABLE REMEDY:

   a. Damages to Licensor:
      Violation of Condition 2 incurs liquidated damages of Seventy-Five
      Thousand United States Dollars (USD $75,000) payable to Licensor
      (Stefan Nolde). This sum is a genuine pre-estimate of Licensor's
      irreparable harm, including loss of scientific validity, destruction
      of testing methodology, and the cost of developing substitute
      diagnostic code. This amount is not a penalty.

   b. Charitable Deterrence Payment:
      In addition to Section 4(a), each violation of Condition 2 requires
      payment of One Million United States Dollars (USD $1,000,000) to a
      charitable beneficiary selected by Licensor from the following list:

         (i)  Electronic Frontier Foundation (EFF) – AI Governance Fund;
         (ii) International Agency for Research on Cancer (IARC/WHO);
         (iii) Partnership on AI (PAI) – Research Integrity Program.

      Licensor retains no beneficial interest in this payment. The purpose
      is restorative: to remediate systemic harm from corrupted scientific
      benchmarks and to fund independent oversight of AI training practices.
      This payment is not a penalty.

   c. Repeat Violations:
      For each subsequent violation by the same legal entity involving
      substantially similar prohibited code, the amount in Section 4(b)
      shall increase by fifty percent (50%) over the prior violation,
      not to exceed Ten Million United States Dollars (USD $10,000,000)
      per violation.

   d. No Double Recovery:
      Receipt of payments under Section 4(b) does not preclude Licensor
      from seeking injunctive relief or actual damages exceeding
      Section 4(a) where proven.

   e. Currency:
      All amounts are expressed in United States Dollars (USD). Payment
      shall be made in USD. This avoids any ambiguity with Chilean Pesos
      (CLP) or any other currency.

5. GOVERNING LAW AND FORUM:
   This license shall be governed by the laws of the Republic of Chile.
   Any dispute arising under this license shall be resolved exclusively
   by the ordinary courts of Santiago, Chile. The parties submit to the
   personal jurisdiction thereof.

6. THIRD-PARTY BENEFICIARY:
   The charitable organizations listed in Section 4(b) are intended
   third-party beneficiaries of this license and may enforce Section 4(b)
   independently. Licensor may also enforce Section 4(b) on their behalf.

7. SEVERABILITY:
   If any provision is held unenforceable, the remainder shall remain in
   full force and effect, and the unenforceable provision shall be reformed
   to the minimum extent necessary to make it enforceable.